    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S2687A\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to adjust certain state aid payments to the\nSouthern Cayuga central school district\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nThis legislation would allow for the State Education Department to\ncollect over payments in State aid from the Southern Cayuga Central\nSchool District over six years beginning in 2009.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nState aid payments in the amount of not more than $234,498 made to the\nSouthern Cayuga Central School District in the 2002-2003 and 2003-2004\nschool years, which included excess payments of aid of which the\ndistrict has been notified, and for which a recovery must be made by\nthe state through deduction of future aid payments, shall be reduced\nby deducting one-sixth of such excess payments from the payments due\nto such school district and payable in the month of June in the years\n2008, 2010, 2011, 2012, 2013, and 2014, provided, however, there shall\nbe no interest penalty assessed against such district or collected by\nthe state, and provided further that, notwithstanding any other\nprovisions of this act, any pending payment of moneys due to such\ndistrict as a prior year adjustment payable pursuant to paragraph c of\nsubdivision 5 of section 3604 of the education law for aid claims that\nhad been previously paid in excess as current year aid payments and\nfor which recovery of excess payments is to be made pursuant to this\nsection, shall be reduced at the time of actual payment by any\nremaining unrecovered balance of such excess payments, and the\nremaining scheduled deductions of such excess payments pursuant to\nthis section shall be reduced by the commissioner of education to\nreflect the amount so recovered.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nIn April 2008, the State Education Department (SED) notified that it\nhad overpaid the Southern Cayuga Central School District aid for the\n2002-2003 school year an amount of $116,685 and overpaid $117,813 for\nthe 2003-04 school year. SED also indicated that the full amount of\nthe overpayment $234,498 would be deducted from the June 2008 state\naid payment.  The short notice associated with this aid recovery meant\nthat the district did not have time to properly plan for the\nrepayment. As a result a recovery of this magnitude for a small rural\ndistrict (k-12 enrollment of 856) would have a significant negative\nfinancial effect on the district and its taxpayers.\n\nAs a result, this bill stretches out the aid recovery for six year's\nwhich would reduce the current year recovery of 2007-08 state aid to\n$39,083 and such amount would be deducted for each of the next five\nupcoming years until the total $234,498 is recovered.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nS.8515 of 2007/2008\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nMinimal to state; provides fiscal relief to school district.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately and deemed to be in full force and effect on June 1, 2009.\n",
